<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the release build. Applied by .github/workflows/release.yml
  when it re-signs the bundle; `deno desktop` applies none of its own.

  allow-jit is not optional: signing with a real Developer ID turns on the
  Hardened Runtime, and under Hardened Runtime mmap(MAP_JIT) is denied without
  this entitlement. V8 can't reserve its executable CodeRange and aborts before
  the window ever opens — which is exactly how v0.1.1 shipped and died:

    # Fatal process out of memory: Failed to reserve virtual memory for CodeRange

  Verified by A/B on an otherwise identical bundle: without this key the app
  aborts at V8 init, with it the app starts and serves.

  Kept to this single key deliberately. Every entitlement here weakens the
  Hardened Runtime, so nothing goes in without a demonstrated failure behind it.
  In particular the app does NOT need:

  - disable-library-validation — a real Developer ID gives laufey_webview and
    libruntime.dylib the same Team ID, so library validation passes. It is only
    needed for locally ad-hoc-signed builds, which have no Team ID at all.
  - allow-unsigned-executable-memory — allow-jit alone is sufficient; V8 uses
    MAP_JIT rather than unsigned executable pages.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
